hat would help labs with the  setup of this or similar workflows  that's an interesting question we are  we're happy to share studies protocols  uh reference materials and of course  we're happy to elaborate on them  however to be compliant with regulations  uh i i need to point out that the actual  validation of laboratory developed tests  uh has to be  independently carried out by any lab  that is  essentially seeking to implement these  ldt's into their lab environment  but  lightening that burden for labs with  access to  ngs and aerys cloud and and enabling  them to generate pathogen data with  essentially the same accuracy as our  vienna based ngs lab that was in fact  one of the main motivations for us and  has remained one of the main motivations  for us to publish and share  the validation results protocols and so  on for the essays that we developed at  aries genetics  perfect thank you  i can see there's another question that  has come  in just now  yes i can  our next question is what is the  accuracy of predictive ast was it  correlated with the ast done at labs  yeah yeah this is a very good question  and sorry if that wasn't clear enough in  the presentation  uh this is in fact correct the accuracy  of predictive ast is measured in terms  of  um agreement with phenotypic traditional  ast  conducted under controlled uh  standardized conditions in clinical labs  so this is how we determine the accuracy  also the study i was referencing uh in  which we performed a multi-center  evaluation of predictive ast  is comparing the results of the  prediction with the  [Music]  phenotypic results conducted as i said  under controlled conditions in a lab so  it's very much a comparison of in  silicon generated results with lab  results and in this case we give the lab  results the benefit of the doubt and are  assuming that uh  they are the ground truth for the  purpose of this evaluation  perfect thank you  thank you again dr materna for your time  today and your